  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022 Life-saving Emergency Livelihood Response in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to protect the livelihoods of the most vulnerable households and increase their food production. This FAO project 1) provides 240,000 people with agricultural inputs (items/packages/kits), 2) vaccinates 1,000,000 animals and 3) provides 199,800 people with livestock inputs (animal feed/live animals, kits, etc.). The project provides life-saving assistance to 379,800 people, including 197,497 women, 106,343 men and 75,960 children.</narrative>
  </description>
